1
00:00:35,076 --> 00:00:40,206
This photo is enough evidence
for us to investigate Senator Quintin.

2
00:00:40,290 --> 00:00:42,292
- What do you think?
- I'm on the fence.

3
00:00:42,375 --> 00:00:48,965
I suggest that we gather stronger evidence
to make it all add up.

4
00:00:52,594 --> 00:00:55,263
Why don't you throw in some corn soup too

5
00:00:55,346 --> 00:00:57,515
to match how corny you are?

6
00:00:57,599 --> 00:01:00,685
Wow, Chiara, your maid of honor
is like a real judge.

7
00:01:00,769 --> 00:01:02,228
She's always passing judgment.

8
00:01:03,271 --> 00:01:07,192
Of course. Because I only want
what's best for my friend.

9
00:01:12,655 --> 00:01:14,574
Between you and Chiara,

10
00:01:14,657 --> 00:01:16,493
you're the one who needs
more preparation for the wedding.

11
00:01:16,576 --> 00:01:19,120
Chiara has class naturally.

12
00:01:19,204 --> 00:01:22,457
But you… You look like you fix
illegal electrical connections.

13
00:01:22,540 --> 00:01:25,168
- Ouch!
- That's harsh.

14
00:01:27,962 --> 00:01:30,381
You might benefit too if you help us.

15
00:01:30,465 --> 00:01:33,426
If you really need my help,
I will help you.

16
00:01:33,510 --> 00:01:38,014
But I need you to do me a favor
before I help you.

17
00:01:42,977 --> 00:01:44,354
Where are we going Captain Pepe?

18
00:01:44,437 --> 00:01:46,689
For sure, you're going
to like this tailor.

19
00:01:46,773 --> 00:01:48,358
High-respected people are his customers.

20
00:01:48,441 --> 00:01:49,275
Who are they?

21
00:01:49,359 --> 00:01:52,320
Mayor, barangay officials,
congressman, and governor.

22
00:01:52,403 --> 00:01:53,780
What's the name of that shop?

23
00:01:55,031 --> 00:01:57,200
Come on, let me introduce you!

24
00:01:58,159 --> 00:02:00,620
You said you'd take me
to your legendary tailor.

25
00:02:01,663 --> 00:02:03,289
Turns out he dresses the dead.

26
00:02:03,998 --> 00:02:05,750
It's basically the same, Mikoy.

27
00:02:05,834 --> 00:02:07,961
The only difference is,
you're still breathing.

28
00:02:08,044 --> 00:02:09,671
The dead aren't.

29
00:02:10,255 --> 00:02:11,214
Wow.

30
00:02:11,297 --> 00:02:12,715
That's not the same.

31
00:02:13,508 --> 00:02:14,968
Where is this tailor?

32
00:02:15,677 --> 00:02:17,303
I can't stay here any longer.

33
00:02:19,139 --> 00:02:21,057
True.

34
00:02:21,141 --> 00:02:22,642
What's your tailor's name again?

35
00:02:24,227 --> 00:02:26,229
Sweet. Sweet. That's the name.

36
00:02:26,312 --> 00:02:28,189
- Sweet?
- There's a corpse!

37
00:02:29,732 --> 00:02:32,152
There's a corpse!

38
00:02:32,235 --> 00:02:34,112
What corpse? It's moving.

39
00:02:35,113 --> 00:02:38,283
Will you keep it down? I was sleeping!

40
00:02:40,201 --> 00:02:41,077
You?

41
00:02:42,954 --> 00:02:44,372
You're the neighborhood watchman, right?

42
00:02:45,081 --> 00:02:46,708
This is my daytime side hustle.

43
00:02:48,084 --> 00:02:49,002
Is that so?

44
00:02:50,503 --> 00:02:51,921
Where's Sweet?

45
00:02:52,589 --> 00:02:55,091
Sorry, they sleep pretty deeply.

46
00:02:59,429 --> 00:03:01,389
- In there?
- Sweet.

47
00:03:10,106 --> 00:03:11,107
You're Sweet?

48
00:03:14,360 --> 00:03:16,070
You used to be an escort,
and now you're a muse?

49
00:03:21,075 --> 00:03:21,951
See?

50
00:03:22,035 --> 00:03:25,121
Looking so fresh, absolutely fresh.

51
00:03:25,204 --> 00:03:27,957
Mikoy, this is the one I told you about.

52
00:03:30,668 --> 00:03:31,920
She's an amazing tailor.

53
00:03:38,593 --> 00:03:42,180
Before you even get to the venue,
you'll already have accent flowers.

54
00:03:42,263 --> 00:03:45,183
They're gorgeous. So refreshing!

55
00:03:45,266 --> 00:03:46,226
There!

56
00:03:48,353 --> 00:03:49,312
I think

57
00:03:49,979 --> 00:03:53,566
this would look beautiful
in your bouquet, Chiara.

58
00:03:58,738 --> 00:04:00,782
They brighten up the whole place.

59
00:04:03,034 --> 00:04:06,746
Out here, we'll serve
the cocktails, of course,

60
00:04:06,829 --> 00:04:13,002
while your guests watch
the sunset between those mountains

61
00:04:13,086 --> 00:04:15,546
surrounded by vibrant,

62
00:04:15,630 --> 00:04:18,258
colorful flowers to brighten their day.

63
00:04:24,931 --> 00:04:26,224
Again?

64
00:04:26,307 --> 00:04:27,433
Another "no"?

65
00:04:27,517 --> 00:04:29,269
When are you ever going to say yes?

66
00:04:29,352 --> 00:04:31,562
It feels like every suggestion I make,

67
00:04:31,646 --> 00:04:33,022
you shoot down.

68
00:04:33,648 --> 00:04:36,943
You know what?
At this point, I'll be the maid of honor.

69
00:04:37,026 --> 00:04:38,778
You be the wedding planner.

70
00:04:38,861 --> 00:04:42,115
I'll just sit inside
and enjoy the reception.

71
00:04:42,198 --> 00:04:43,908
My point is,

72
00:04:43,992 --> 00:04:46,286
the bride's bouquet should be symbolic.

73
00:04:46,369 --> 00:04:49,539
After all, it's the only thing
she carries down the aisle

74
00:04:49,622 --> 00:04:52,500
before she steps into
the next chapter of her life.

75
00:04:52,583 --> 00:04:56,546
They're not just flowers
to match the wedding colors.

76
00:04:56,629 --> 00:05:00,341
The flowers should reflect
the bride's story.

77
00:05:01,342 --> 00:05:05,513
Don't give me all that symbolism
and hidden-meaning stuff.

78
00:05:05,596 --> 00:05:07,015
I know a thing or two.

79
00:05:07,098 --> 00:05:09,142
According to Greek mythology,

80
00:05:09,225 --> 00:05:13,479
Clytie loved Apollo with all her heart.

81
00:05:13,563 --> 00:05:18,318
She transformed into a flower
that could follow the sun god.

82
00:05:18,401 --> 00:05:20,111
Isn't that touching?

83
00:05:20,820 --> 00:05:22,864
That's true love!

84
00:05:22,947 --> 00:05:26,075
Guess what kind of flower follows the sun?

85
00:05:29,912 --> 00:05:31,581
That's right! Perfect!

86
00:05:34,876 --> 00:05:36,919
Thanks for the answer
you probably got from the Internet,

87
00:05:37,003 --> 00:05:38,588
but you're missing some details.

88
00:05:40,673 --> 00:05:42,800
Clytie's love for Apollo was unrequited.

89
00:05:42,884 --> 00:05:45,178
The sun god loved someone else.

90
00:05:45,887 --> 00:05:50,016
So if you think about it, it was more
of an obsession than devotion.

91
00:05:51,601 --> 00:05:53,561
Imagine turning yourself into a flower

92
00:05:53,644 --> 00:05:56,272
just so you could keep following
and staring at the sun forever.

93
00:05:56,856 --> 00:05:58,858
That's just masochistic, isn't it?

94
00:05:58,941 --> 00:06:02,945
Chiara, are you going to a wedding
or walking into your own misery?

95
00:06:05,239 --> 00:06:07,283
I'm not a masochist either.

96
00:06:08,076 --> 00:06:11,746
And I can devote myself to Mikoy
because I love him so much,

97
00:06:11,829 --> 00:06:15,917
but if he stops loving me,
and falls for someone else…

98
00:06:16,626 --> 00:06:19,420
It would definitely hurt, but…

99
00:06:20,046 --> 00:06:21,672
I'll move on eventually.

100
00:06:26,135 --> 00:06:28,846
If not sunflowers, then what flower?

101
00:06:32,016 --> 00:06:35,353
Wow, going for the Kate Middleton look?

102
00:06:35,436 --> 00:06:37,146
You just looked that up online too.

103
00:06:37,230 --> 00:06:39,774
At least it's better than
the stuff you search online.

104
00:06:40,691 --> 00:06:42,193
Lily of the Valley has a deeper meaning.

105
00:06:46,614 --> 00:06:48,950
You can't change the past,

106
00:06:49,033 --> 00:06:51,452
but you can still allow yourself
to be happy again,

107
00:06:51,536 --> 00:06:53,329
especially once you've found it.

108
00:07:00,128 --> 00:07:01,337
Just like Mikoy and me.

109
00:07:03,756 --> 00:07:07,802
I thought I'd be trapped
in the darkness forever.

110
00:07:08,678 --> 00:07:12,056
Then he came
and brought color back into my world.

111
00:07:13,766 --> 00:07:16,811
I think I've found
the perfect bouquet for my wedding.

112
00:07:17,895 --> 00:07:20,356
You're the perfect maid of honor, Alex.

113
00:07:34,954 --> 00:07:38,666
Here's number 23. Next is 24.

114
00:07:39,250 --> 00:07:41,752
Bro, what kind of place is this?

115
00:07:41,836 --> 00:07:42,920
Should we try somewhere else?

116
00:07:43,588 --> 00:07:44,589
Or

117
00:07:44,672 --> 00:07:46,632
just shop online. Free shipping too.

118
00:07:46,716 --> 00:07:48,342
- Yes.
- Sounds good.

119
00:07:48,426 --> 00:07:51,179
You handsome guys.

120
00:07:51,262 --> 00:07:54,056
We haven't even reached
the exciting part yet.

121
00:07:54,140 --> 00:07:59,645
The most important thing
is taking your measurements!

122
00:07:59,729 --> 00:08:05,693
Because that's the foundation
of a perfectly fitted suit.

123
00:08:05,776 --> 00:08:06,944
You guys, honestly,

124
00:08:07,570 --> 00:08:09,864
you're seriously lacking in patience.

125
00:08:11,407 --> 00:08:14,243
You know, Tailor Sweet is right.

126
00:08:14,327 --> 00:08:15,745
Patience is a virtue.

127
00:08:15,828 --> 00:08:17,288
Just relax, okay?

128
00:08:17,371 --> 00:08:19,123
- Let's try this first.
- Patience.

129
00:08:19,207 --> 00:08:21,334
Seeing is believing.

130
00:08:23,044 --> 00:08:24,754
Seeing is believing, huh?

131
00:08:24,837 --> 00:08:26,631
Well then, here you go.

132
00:08:27,673 --> 00:08:28,716
Take a look.

133
00:08:33,513 --> 00:08:34,347
Mikoy!

134
00:08:34,972 --> 00:08:37,808
- That's you!
- All natural, no chemicals added.

135
00:08:37,892 --> 00:08:39,477
- Let me see.
- That's really you!

136
00:08:40,603 --> 00:08:41,687
- That's just the beginning!
- Awesome!

137
00:08:41,771 --> 00:08:42,813
Here's another one.

138
00:08:45,525 --> 00:08:47,109
That looks like us!

139
00:08:47,193 --> 00:08:48,194
That's us!

140
00:08:48,277 --> 00:08:49,529
There's Jan-Jan!

141
00:08:49,612 --> 00:08:50,613
Still smells like sunshine!

142
00:08:50,696 --> 00:08:51,739
That's me.

143
00:08:51,822 --> 00:08:52,865
Beautiful!

144
00:08:52,949 --> 00:08:54,367
Handsome!

145
00:08:54,450 --> 00:08:55,368
See?

146
00:08:55,451 --> 00:08:57,954
I told you I'm a magician.

147
00:08:58,037 --> 00:08:59,997
I'm just getting started.

148
00:09:00,081 --> 00:09:02,333
I've even got someone who's half Spanish.

149
00:09:02,416 --> 00:09:04,460
Half Filipino, half Spanish.

150
00:09:04,544 --> 00:09:07,463
They trusted me to make
their wedding outfits,

151
00:09:07,547 --> 00:09:10,550
along with the attire
for the entire entourage.

152
00:09:10,633 --> 00:09:11,968
Just like you, Tailor!

153
00:09:12,051 --> 00:09:12,843
That's right!

154
00:09:12,927 --> 00:09:14,428
Half Filipino, half Filipina!

155
00:09:16,347 --> 00:09:18,891
No, but this was the style back then.

156
00:09:18,975 --> 00:09:21,269
Our grandmothers used
to starch our clothes,

157
00:09:21,352 --> 00:09:24,397
then it will be styled.

158
00:09:24,480 --> 00:09:26,816
Like this?

159
00:09:26,899 --> 00:09:28,651
You all look completely transformed!

160
00:09:28,734 --> 00:09:30,027
See?

161
00:09:30,111 --> 00:09:32,572
Tailoring is no joke.

162
00:09:32,655 --> 00:09:36,784
Every detail matters
to a meticulous groom,

163
00:09:36,867 --> 00:09:40,121
from the fabric down to the buttons.

164
00:09:40,204 --> 00:09:41,038
Right?

165
00:09:41,122 --> 00:09:44,917
It may be challenging,
but it's always worth it.

166
00:09:45,001 --> 00:09:46,752
Okay, fine.

167
00:09:46,836 --> 00:09:48,129
I see your vision now.

168
00:09:48,212 --> 00:09:50,506
Well then, in that case,
we're all getting our suits made here.

169
00:09:50,590 --> 00:09:51,924
Right here.

170
00:09:52,008 --> 00:09:52,967
- Yes!
- Deal?

171
00:09:53,050 --> 00:09:55,553
Okay, agree!

172
00:09:55,636 --> 00:09:58,097
Just for you.

173
00:09:58,180 --> 00:10:00,099
Go ahead and take our measurements.

174
00:10:00,182 --> 00:10:01,017
Measure us already.

175
00:10:01,100 --> 00:10:01,976
Twenty-eight.

176
00:10:02,059 --> 00:10:03,269
Seven inches.

177
00:10:03,352 --> 00:10:05,479
One peso around, eight in length.
Like that.

178
00:10:05,563 --> 00:10:08,065
Trapped it.

179
00:10:10,651 --> 00:10:13,571
Should we do the favor Viktor asked of us?

180
00:10:14,614 --> 00:10:16,866
It seems impossible.

181
00:10:17,992 --> 00:10:18,993
You're right.

182
00:10:20,202 --> 00:10:22,413
I'm having second thoughts too.

183
00:10:27,168 --> 00:10:28,336
It's still risky.

184
00:10:29,253 --> 00:10:31,797
He's a Moraviano.
He thinks like the mafia.

185
00:10:31,881 --> 00:10:34,258
Today he's asking us for a favor,

186
00:10:34,342 --> 00:10:36,344
tomorrow he'll have us
wrapped around his finger.

187
00:10:37,053 --> 00:10:38,679
We still need to be careful.

188
00:10:40,014 --> 00:10:40,931
I know.

189
00:10:41,891 --> 00:10:43,351
But we've already gone this far.

190
00:10:43,434 --> 00:10:45,436
We've already talked to him.

191
00:10:45,519 --> 00:10:48,105
Now we just have to decide

192
00:10:48,189 --> 00:10:50,483
whether we'll do him the favor or not.

193
00:10:51,442 --> 00:10:53,069
And if we do,

194
00:10:53,152 --> 00:10:55,446
no one else can know about it.

195
00:10:59,533 --> 00:11:00,701
What's that?

196
00:11:01,827 --> 00:11:03,496
What are you two talking about?

197
00:11:04,622 --> 00:11:07,833
What is it that no one else can know?

198
00:11:20,054 --> 00:11:24,225
<i>Se, se, se-se, se-cret</i>

199
00:11:24,308 --> 00:11:28,104
<i>It's not something you're supposed to know</i>

200
00:11:28,187 --> 00:11:32,566
<i>Se, se, se-se, se-cret</i>

201
00:11:32,650 --> 00:11:37,321
<i>I'm keeping you in suspense</i>

202
00:11:37,988 --> 00:11:39,657
Cocoy, Carlota, enough.

203
00:11:40,366 --> 00:11:41,784
Stop beating around the bush.

204
00:11:41,867 --> 00:11:43,911
Don't take this conversation
off on a tangent.

205
00:11:43,994 --> 00:11:46,872
What information is it
that no one else should know?

206
00:11:50,626 --> 00:11:53,129
Answer my question, okay?

207
00:11:53,212 --> 00:11:55,089
Just a reminder.

208
00:11:55,172 --> 00:11:57,007
Whatever it is you're planning to do,

209
00:11:57,591 --> 00:11:59,760
I can still send both of you back to jail.

210
00:11:59,844 --> 00:12:02,388
And if you still refuse to tell me,

211
00:12:02,471 --> 00:12:05,266
I can file an insubordination report.

212
00:12:06,559 --> 00:12:07,476
Sean.

213
00:12:07,560 --> 00:12:08,477
Sean?

214
00:12:09,228 --> 00:12:12,982
This isn't about classified information.

215
00:12:14,024 --> 00:12:17,778
And it isn't a matter
of national concern either.

216
00:12:17,862 --> 00:12:19,071
Actually,

217
00:12:19,572 --> 00:12:21,407
it's more of a personal matter.

218
00:12:24,827 --> 00:12:26,871
A personal matter?

219
00:12:29,498 --> 00:12:30,833
Hey, miss.

220
00:12:30,916 --> 00:12:33,085
Let's get one thing straight.

221
00:12:33,169 --> 00:12:35,004
Why do you always have to show off?

222
00:12:35,087 --> 00:12:37,047
What exactly are you trying to do?

223
00:12:37,715 --> 00:12:39,383
I'm not showing off.

224
00:12:39,467 --> 00:12:41,093
I just have information

225
00:12:41,177 --> 00:12:43,637
that could help Chiara
make better decisions.

226
00:12:43,721 --> 00:12:47,349
That's why there's a wedding planner.
To plan the wedding.

227
00:12:47,433 --> 00:12:49,226
And that's why there's a maid of honor.

228
00:12:51,061 --> 00:12:52,771
I'm not just here

229
00:12:52,855 --> 00:12:55,024
to wear a gown
and pose in photos with the bride.

230
00:12:55,107 --> 00:12:57,610
You're so dramatic.

231
00:12:57,693 --> 00:12:59,945
You're taking your role way too seriously.

232
00:13:00,946 --> 00:13:03,240
It's called being efficient.

233
00:13:03,866 --> 00:13:06,202
You can't just serve Chiara
whatever you want

234
00:13:06,285 --> 00:13:07,620
and expect her to go with it.

235
00:13:07,703 --> 00:13:11,207
Again, this is her wedding, not yours.

236
00:13:11,832 --> 00:13:13,709
She deserves options.

237
00:13:13,792 --> 00:13:16,462
Wow, you really won't stop.

238
00:13:20,883 --> 00:13:22,676
What? What?

239
00:13:22,760 --> 00:13:24,512
What? What?

240
00:13:24,595 --> 00:13:25,930
You're impossible.

241
00:13:26,013 --> 00:13:26,931
Come on.

242
00:13:27,014 --> 00:13:28,641
- You jerk!
- What? You can't reach me.

243
00:13:28,724 --> 00:13:29,892
- Let go of me!
- Too short, huh?

244
00:13:31,435 --> 00:13:32,311
What?

245
00:13:34,480 --> 00:13:35,648
You really!

246
00:13:40,528 --> 00:13:41,695
Her!

247
00:13:42,530 --> 00:13:43,781
It's her!

248
00:13:49,745 --> 00:13:51,413
It's Cocoy.

249
00:13:51,497 --> 00:13:54,124
Ever since he found out we've been dating,

250
00:13:54,708 --> 00:13:56,126
he hasn't stopped bothering me.

251
00:13:58,420 --> 00:14:00,965
Cocoy. Why would you do that?

252
00:14:01,048 --> 00:14:03,926
Why do you keep bothering
and cornering Carlota?

253
00:14:04,009 --> 00:14:05,177
Come on!

254
00:14:05,261 --> 00:14:06,762
It's obvious

255
00:14:06,845 --> 00:14:10,224
you're bigger and stronger than me,
and you can rap way better.

256
00:14:10,307 --> 00:14:11,934
But when it comes to this,

257
00:14:12,935 --> 00:14:14,436
I'm not backing down, bro.

258
00:14:18,023 --> 00:14:20,818
<i>Carlota, you're truly captivating</i>

259
00:14:22,570 --> 00:14:23,654
<i>Sean, no</i>

260
00:14:23,737 --> 00:14:25,197
<i>You've got it all wrong</i>

261
00:14:29,410 --> 00:14:32,162
<i>You know we're GAGO agents</i>

262
00:14:32,246 --> 00:14:34,164
<i>We're all handsome dudes</i>

263
00:14:36,166 --> 00:14:38,294
What I meant was,

264
00:14:38,377 --> 00:14:41,380
Cocoy wouldn't stop bothering me,

265
00:14:41,463 --> 00:14:45,342
trying to prove he had memorized

266
00:14:45,426 --> 00:14:50,180
- <i>The 7 Habits of Highly Effective People</i>.
- <i>Effective People</i>.

267
00:14:50,264 --> 00:14:51,307
See?

268
00:14:52,725 --> 00:14:53,726
All right, all right.

269
00:14:53,809 --> 00:14:56,854
When it comes to
<i>The 7 Habits of Highly Effective People</i>,

270
00:14:56,937 --> 00:14:57,897
that's my specialty.

271
00:14:57,980 --> 00:15:01,025
When it comes to that, I never back down.

272
00:15:01,108 --> 00:15:02,359
See? I told you!

273
00:15:02,443 --> 00:15:04,987
- That's exactly what I told Cocoy.
- Yep, you did.

274
00:15:05,070 --> 00:15:09,074
When it comes to
<i>The 7 Habits of Highly Effective People</i>,

275
00:15:09,158 --> 00:15:11,493
you're the only person I know
who has truly mastered it.

276
00:15:11,577 --> 00:15:15,581
<i>The 7 Habits of Highly Effective People</i>.

277
00:15:15,664 --> 00:15:19,084
Even in your sleep,
you know its essence by heart.

278
00:15:19,168 --> 00:15:20,127
Only you.

279
00:15:22,379 --> 00:15:25,674
Wow, I've influenced so many people
here at the office.

280
00:15:26,550 --> 00:15:29,094
Of course. I live by what I master.

281
00:15:29,178 --> 00:15:30,638
- Okay?
- There you go!

282
00:15:30,721 --> 00:15:32,139
That's my strength.

283
00:15:32,222 --> 00:15:34,183
That's why I'm so effective.

284
00:15:49,573 --> 00:15:54,161
I brought you two here
to help reduce my stress.

285
00:15:54,870 --> 00:15:58,624
Instead, you're competing
to be the bigger bridezilla.

286
00:16:03,629 --> 00:16:05,214
You didn't become a bridezilla.

287
00:16:07,633 --> 00:16:10,511
You're the one who never shuts up.

288
00:16:10,594 --> 00:16:11,845
Whatever.

289
00:16:11,929 --> 00:16:15,099
I won't stay silent
when I know I can help.

290
00:16:15,683 --> 00:16:19,520
But you never stay silent when you should,

291
00:16:19,603 --> 00:16:20,604
so shut up.

292
00:16:29,780 --> 00:16:31,865
If you two can't make up,

293
00:16:32,658 --> 00:16:35,244
maybe I should just fire both of you.

294
00:16:41,375 --> 00:16:44,336
You're still not making up?

295
00:16:46,922 --> 00:16:49,299
Fine. I'll be the bigger person.

296
00:16:49,967 --> 00:16:51,010
Oh, wow.

297
00:16:51,093 --> 00:16:52,970
No, I'll do it.

298
00:16:53,053 --> 00:16:55,389
I'll be the bigger person.

299
00:16:55,472 --> 00:16:57,224
Fine, go ahead.

300
00:17:00,019 --> 00:17:03,564
I won't get offended anymore
by your suggestions.

301
00:17:04,440 --> 00:17:06,650
But promise me

302
00:17:06,734 --> 00:17:09,111
that your words
won't be offensive anymore.

303
00:17:09,862 --> 00:17:11,321
Don't make them insulting.

304
00:17:12,531 --> 00:17:14,366
Not hurtful.

305
00:17:15,784 --> 00:17:19,955
All right. I apologize
if that's how I came across.

306
00:17:21,874 --> 00:17:23,542
I really just wanted to help.

307
00:17:26,336 --> 00:17:27,880
I just want what's best for her.

308
00:17:30,924 --> 00:17:32,301
Okay, I get it now.

309
00:17:32,384 --> 00:17:34,553
Turns out we want the same thing.

310
00:17:35,804 --> 00:17:37,056
So, are we good?

311
00:17:51,987 --> 00:17:53,530
You two made up?

312
00:17:54,281 --> 00:17:56,366
Yes, but my knee still hurts.

313
00:17:56,450 --> 00:17:57,284
Oh, wrong one.

314
00:17:57,367 --> 00:17:58,952
No, both of them.

315
00:18:01,288 --> 00:18:02,831
That was intense.

316
00:18:09,671 --> 00:18:11,715
- Wow!
- There!

317
00:18:13,967 --> 00:18:17,387
You're so sweet, sweetheart!

318
00:18:17,471 --> 00:18:18,347
Come on, let's eat.

319
00:18:19,765 --> 00:18:21,391
Go ahead and eat, sweetheart.

320
00:18:27,981 --> 00:18:30,734
Are you okay? You seem…
You seem a little down.

321
00:18:35,114 --> 00:18:39,952
Lord, thank You for the blessings
You have given us today.

322
00:18:45,582 --> 00:18:46,708
Let's eat!

323
00:18:46,792 --> 00:18:48,418
Dig in!

324
00:18:48,502 --> 00:18:50,796
What are you doing?

325
00:18:51,839 --> 00:18:54,716
What else? I'm about to share
in the Lord's blessings.

326
00:18:56,009 --> 00:18:58,178
Mikoy, I don't think you're invited.

327
00:18:58,262 --> 00:18:59,138
Why not?

328
00:18:59,721 --> 00:19:01,640
Buddy, you've already got a love life.

329
00:19:01,723 --> 00:19:03,100
Don't get too greedy with your blessings.

330
00:19:03,183 --> 00:19:04,017
Exactly!

331
00:19:04,101 --> 00:19:05,310
- That's right.
- Exactly.

332
00:19:05,394 --> 00:19:07,062
Come on, what's that got to do
with anything?

333
00:19:08,397 --> 00:19:10,566
What answer do you want? The truth?

334
00:19:10,649 --> 00:19:12,109
A lie.

335
00:19:12,818 --> 00:19:13,861
Obviously, the truth.

336
00:19:13,944 --> 00:19:14,820
Of course.

337
00:19:14,903 --> 00:19:16,071
Rahmboy, tell him.

338
00:19:16,155 --> 00:19:17,364
Tell me what?

339
00:19:17,447 --> 00:19:18,824
Bro,

340
00:19:18,907 --> 00:19:21,285
I hate to be the bearer of bad news, but…

341
00:19:21,368 --> 00:19:24,204
The guys and I talked it over,
all us boys.

342
00:19:24,288 --> 00:19:25,247
Go on.

343
00:19:25,330 --> 00:19:27,249
For your wedding,

344
00:19:28,333 --> 00:19:31,587
you're about ten kilos over the limit.

345
00:19:35,716 --> 00:19:37,176
What is this, a bridge?

346
00:19:37,259 --> 00:19:38,343
That has a weight limit?

347
00:19:39,344 --> 00:19:40,470
You guys are unbelievable.

348
00:19:42,514 --> 00:19:44,516
- We're just looking out for you, bro.
- Yes.

349
00:19:44,600 --> 00:19:45,893
You're the star of the day.

350
00:19:45,976 --> 00:19:48,562
Among all the handsome guys,
you're the general!

351
00:19:48,645 --> 00:19:50,272
- You have to look fit.
- This is delicious!

352
00:19:50,355 --> 00:19:52,274
So delicious!

353
00:19:52,357 --> 00:19:55,527
There's even salted eggs!

354
00:20:00,407 --> 00:20:01,742
You know,

355
00:20:01,825 --> 00:20:04,286
my confidence is completely shot today.

356
00:20:04,369 --> 00:20:05,495
And then,

357
00:20:05,579 --> 00:20:07,706
you laughed too.

358
00:20:08,415 --> 00:20:11,418
No, I wasn't laughing.

359
00:20:12,044 --> 00:20:16,590
I just found your friends
really amusing, sweetheart.

360
00:20:17,216 --> 00:20:18,926
Besides,

361
00:20:20,177 --> 00:20:24,264
you don't have to change anything
for our wedding.

362
00:20:26,350 --> 00:20:30,562
You don't have to make yourself suffer
just because of our wedding.

363
00:20:32,105 --> 00:20:35,817
It's not that I'm making myself suffer
or punishing myself.

364
00:20:36,443 --> 00:20:39,696
I'm just saying Rahmboy does have a point.

365
00:20:42,658 --> 00:20:45,035
And one day, when I'm lying in my coffin…

366
00:20:46,828 --> 00:20:48,497
What are you talking about?

367
00:20:49,581 --> 00:20:53,543
I mean, one day,
I don't want to look back with regrets.

368
00:20:54,419 --> 00:20:56,922
You know what I mean?

369
00:20:57,005 --> 00:20:59,633
That I wasn't the best version of myself

370
00:21:00,467 --> 00:21:02,219
when I met you at the altar.

371
00:21:03,762 --> 00:21:05,180
I don't want that.

372
00:21:22,155 --> 00:21:23,615
You know, you're sweet too, sweetheart.

373
00:21:25,409 --> 00:21:27,035
But nothing's stopping me now.

374
00:21:27,119 --> 00:21:28,578
I'm going on a diet!

375
00:21:28,662 --> 00:21:31,081
I promise, sweetheart. This is for you.

376
00:21:34,626 --> 00:21:36,461
Are you sure you're skipping dinner?

377
00:21:36,545 --> 00:21:37,754
Of course I'm eating!

378
00:21:40,299 --> 00:21:41,591
Come on.

379
00:21:41,675 --> 00:21:42,676
Go ahead and eat.

380
00:21:43,927 --> 00:21:45,095
You're really not eating?

381
00:22:17,544 --> 00:22:18,837
How's it going over there, Bok?

382
00:22:19,504 --> 00:22:21,590
Need backup? Just let me know.

383
00:22:23,091 --> 00:22:25,427
I'm good here, Bok. You can relax.

384
00:22:30,265 --> 00:22:32,893
What were you expecting
when you went there?

385
00:22:32,976 --> 00:22:36,188
Another heart-pounding,
action-packed adventure?

386
00:22:36,980 --> 00:22:39,524
Not really. Those get exhausting too.

387
00:22:39,608 --> 00:22:43,820
<i>But I do miss</i>
<i>the adrenaline rush sometimes.</i>

388
00:22:44,404 --> 00:22:48,158
Actually, I welcome
this refreshing chapter.

389
00:22:49,159 --> 00:22:51,453
It's refreshing to see

390
00:22:51,536 --> 00:22:54,790
that the normal life Mikoy and Chiara
have always dreamed of is possible.

391
00:22:55,791 --> 00:23:00,462
And it's nice knowing you're getting
to witness all of it. Okay?

392
00:23:00,545 --> 00:23:02,839
<i>It's a nice change</i>
<i>of pace for you too, Bok.</i>

393
00:23:02,923 --> 00:23:04,257
<i>And remember.</i>

394
00:23:04,341 --> 00:23:07,219
You deserve
a regulated nervous system too.

395
00:23:07,928 --> 00:23:09,638
We all do, Bok.

396
00:23:09,721 --> 00:23:12,432
We can't spend our whole lives
stuck in survival mode.

397
00:23:14,518 --> 00:23:16,186
This is what you should focus on, Bok.

398
00:23:16,937 --> 00:23:18,814
The main mission that brought you there.

399
00:23:18,897 --> 00:23:22,109
<i>Be the best maid of honor ever!</i>

400
00:23:24,611 --> 00:23:25,654
Copy, Bok.

401
00:23:40,127 --> 00:23:41,336
Sofie.

402
00:23:42,504 --> 00:23:43,380
Are you still at school?

403
00:23:47,968 --> 00:23:50,095
Hey, bro. Where do you want to go?

404
00:23:50,178 --> 00:23:51,680
- Are they coming too?
- Probably not.

405
00:23:53,515 --> 00:23:55,976
Want to grab a midnight snack?

406
00:23:57,602 --> 00:23:58,937
She probably already ate.

407
00:23:59,771 --> 00:24:01,064
She'll probably say no.

408
00:24:08,446 --> 00:24:09,447
Hey.

409
00:24:10,323 --> 00:24:12,200
I'm still at school.

410
00:24:12,909 --> 00:24:14,327
Come keep me company.

411
00:24:22,210 --> 00:24:23,962
Come keep me company.

412
00:24:25,213 --> 00:24:26,923
No, that's too casual.

413
00:24:27,549 --> 00:24:29,342
It sounds too demanding.

414
00:24:29,968 --> 00:24:31,553
She might get turned off.

415
00:24:37,809 --> 00:24:39,186
Angelito.

416
00:24:44,608 --> 00:24:46,151
What are you doing? Trying to be funny?

417
00:24:46,902 --> 00:24:48,153
You're not funny.

418
00:24:50,447 --> 00:24:52,741
Hang on, Angelito. I know this. Wait.

419
00:24:55,952 --> 00:24:56,870
Again, again.

420
00:25:22,812 --> 00:25:24,689
You know, Mario,

421
00:25:24,773 --> 00:25:26,107
no offense, but…

422
00:25:26,191 --> 00:25:29,903
being a village watchman doesn't seem like
the most exciting job in the world.

423
00:25:29,986 --> 00:25:31,488
What makes you say that?

424
00:25:33,156 --> 00:25:34,991
It feels like you've never really
experienced much, Mario.

425
00:25:35,075 --> 00:25:36,576
Like you've lived a sheltered life.

426
00:25:37,160 --> 00:25:39,079
Whenever I see you, Mario,

427
00:25:39,162 --> 00:25:40,789
you don't strike me as an action guy.

428
00:25:41,748 --> 00:25:44,251
Is there really a proper way
to hold a baton?

429
00:25:45,502 --> 00:25:46,628
Dekyo, Jan,

430
00:25:46,711 --> 00:25:50,048
show Mario the proper way to hold one.

431
00:25:50,131 --> 00:25:52,425
Here, Mario.

432
00:25:53,885 --> 00:25:55,178
Hold it.

433
00:26:04,854 --> 00:26:06,606
Mario! Mr. Mario!

434
00:26:06,690 --> 00:26:07,983
There's trouble over there!

435
00:26:19,202 --> 00:26:20,036
Here, let me have that.

436
00:26:45,812 --> 00:26:49,357
What I want to know is,
what did you see during that street fight?

437
00:26:49,441 --> 00:26:50,775
Oh, that.

438
00:26:50,859 --> 00:26:53,445
I'm sorry. I was pretty drunk back then.

439
00:26:54,029 --> 00:26:55,488
Then you're no help at all.

440
00:26:55,572 --> 00:26:57,449
We should've just watched
the CCTV footage.

441
00:26:57,532 --> 00:27:00,368
- There's CCTV?
- Didn't I mention that?

442
00:27:02,495 --> 00:27:05,123
Say goodbye to your hair because for sure,

443
00:27:05,206 --> 00:27:06,333
you'll miss that, you witch!

444
00:27:06,416 --> 00:27:08,293
Let go of me!

445
00:27:11,755 --> 00:27:13,381
Because you're a slut!

446
00:27:13,465 --> 00:27:14,632
You're even more a slut!

447
00:27:17,385 --> 00:27:19,179
It's not even my wedding,

448
00:27:19,262 --> 00:27:21,431
but I'm already tearing up for you.

449
00:27:21,514 --> 00:27:23,308
You look so beautiful!

450
00:27:24,059 --> 00:27:25,518
You're so dramatic.

451
00:27:26,436 --> 00:27:27,937
But it's true, Chiara.

452
00:27:28,021 --> 00:27:30,440
You look radiant. You're glowing.
You look gorgeous!

453
00:27:30,523 --> 00:27:31,566
It suits you perfectly.

454
00:27:34,569 --> 00:27:36,696
How about my plans for our country?

455
00:27:36,780 --> 00:27:37,864
What I'm gonna do is…

456
00:27:39,657 --> 00:27:42,202
To bring the Sinigang Cartel back!
